{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1454365-tier-1-mummy-mummies-in-crossovers","id":1454365,"title":"Tier 1 Mummy/Mummies in Crossovers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-06T10:51:09-07:00","id":1454365,"title":"Tier 1 Mummy/Mummies in Crossovers","content":"So I am of a mind to run a small scale tier 1(maybe tier 2 in the late game) and what I started thinking about which games could be used and my mind came to Mummy and I was like..&quot;no&quot;...and then my mind went to &quot;or could I?&quot;. So that is why I am asking for the Wisdom of the forum...can the Arisen(not immortals, not sadikhs, not cultists, but the arisen themselves), work in a Tier 1 chronicle and by extension could they be in a tier 1 supernatural chronicle without stomping over everyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T13:29:16-07:00","id":1454377,"title":"","content":"One day, I need to do that chat about the purpose of the Arisen's powers in the Chronicles world/idiom and how that relates to crossover, but in the meantime:<br /> <br /> Can they work? Yes. Do you need to plan carefully for them? Yes. Namely, you need to make sure that their interests (whether acting for the judges/guilds or acting independently, often some measure of both) keep in line of the tone of the setting, keep plausible reasons they're isolated from their Arisen peers on the board, and otherwise check out Overly Sarcastic's Trope Talk on Powerhouses and apply the wisdom within as best as you're able.<br /> <br /> I might say more later when I'm not at work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T13:40:15-07:00","id":1454378,"title":"","content":"It may be obvious, but it still needs to be said: Mummies become weaker as their activity cycle continues. You can pit your players against a Mummy at low Sekhem, who lost access to most of their magics, and deals with the fallout of their earier plans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T15:18:23-07:00","id":1454383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1454365-tier-1-mummy-mummies-in-crossovers?p=1454378#post1454378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may be obvious, but it still needs to be said: Mummies become weaker as their activity cycle continues. You can pit your players against a Mummy at low Sekhem, who lost access to most of their magics, and deals with the fallout of their earier plans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I meant as a PC alongside weak/starting vampires, changelings, and so on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T18:00:17-07:00","id":1454400,"title":"","content":"That still works: just start the Arisen with a lower Sekhem than normal. Say that this particular Descent has been a rough one, and he lost a lot of Sekhem before he could gain much in the way of Pillars and Memory. Unless you eventually intend to upgrade the game's tier, the fact that he's gradually getting weaker while his companions are gradually getting stronger isn't going to be much of an issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T05:00:05-07:00","id":1454438,"title":"","content":"I just remembered that there is a type of Mummies that may be useful to you. Mummies with the right balance of obedience and uselessness may be abandoned by their Judge without being additionally punished. They're called Nehu (Mummy 2nd Ed; p.326). They have to make do with their Cults and dictates of Fate to awake, and always Arise with Sekhem 1. Your character could either reach that state on purpose, or by accident. They may not even remember which one that was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-15T22:54:24-07:00","id":1455010,"title":"","content":"I haven't found them to be a problem. Mummies stood out a lot more in 1e, but you can make a dude who just melts everything in line of sight in like half the games now. Really, the way their powers work off a selection of charges that are only regained at a very slow rate, and the way they are on missions that you can slap them with a ruler if they deviate from the plan, make me think you generally won't have many problems with mummies in crossover.<br /> <br /> If you have, say, mages, demons, deviants, and/or beasts, I wouldn't bother even nerfing them at all.<br /> <br /> P.S. what does tier 1 mean in this context? tier 1 hunters and ghouls and stuff? or just the core definition of a street level one? a very local scale chronicle situated by a mummy's tomb and other spoopiness sounds fun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11876,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","user":"Deinos","date":". 07-16-2021, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}